{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01118",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.85,
      "end_seconds": 3.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "morning doctor lovely to meet you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 4.95,
      "end_seconds": 9.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "So of course leave it there. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 13.27,
      "end_seconds": 16.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Thank you for fitting us in, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.3,
      "end_seconds": 23.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "please do extra information is always welcome"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 25.24,
      "end_seconds": 30.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "doctor, it's sudden shortness of breath. That's what we're worried about"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.77,
      "end_seconds": 33.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "is it accompanied by anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.53,
      "end_seconds": 49.43,
      "duration_seconds": 14.9,
      "text": "Erm, when it starts I tend to get sharp pain when I breathe in as well. The sharp pain when I breathe in? That's been for about a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.49,
      "end_seconds": 53.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "Have you been coughing up a little blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 54.34,
      "end_seconds": 57.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "yeah, I've had that since last Tuesday"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.37,
      "end_seconds": 78.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "any chest tightness or wheeze?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 80.44,
      "end_seconds": 83.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "No, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.6,
      "end_seconds": 87.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "and fever, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.56,
      "end_seconds": 90.22,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Definitely no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 91.75,
      "end_seconds": 97.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.65,
      "text": "actually you know doctor I did notice fever she doesn't always say"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.98,
      "end_seconds": 104.57,
      "duration_seconds": 6.59,
      "text": "no, I don't think I did maybe a little, I'm not sure"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.25,
      "end_seconds": 114.03,
      "duration_seconds": 8.78,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Anything on the skin I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.65,
      "end_seconds": 119.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "nothing on the skin, um, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.49,
      "end_seconds": 123.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.58,
      "end_seconds": 127.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "I move fine otherwise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.27,
      "end_seconds": 132.66,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Have you been to to theatre before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.58,
      "end_seconds": 137.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Just an operation for a hernia, last spring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.34,
      "end_seconds": 143.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "what does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.81,
      "end_seconds": 148.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.08,
      "end_seconds": 150.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.14,
      "end_seconds": 154.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "My partner and our baby"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.84,
      "end_seconds": 164.18,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "have you got any known allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.54,
      "end_seconds": 175.4,
      "duration_seconds": 9.86,
      "text": "I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 176.89,
      "end_seconds": 180.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.49,
      "end_seconds": 183.98,
      "duration_seconds": 1.49,
      "text": "yes, acid reflux"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.09,
      "end_seconds": 190.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.51,
      "text": "I follow okay, are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 191.11,
      "end_seconds": 195.34,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "it's omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.89,
      "end_seconds": 213.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "Let me get the readings out of the way."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.31,
      "end_seconds": 228.06,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "okay sit still for a moment.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 245.14,
      "end_seconds": 256.69,
      "duration_seconds": 11.55,
      "text": "Okay: SpO2 90 percent on room air, pressure 134 over 89, respiratory rate 21, pulse is 90 beats a minute, temperature 36.7."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.59,
      "end_seconds": 260.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "is that normal?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.8,
      "end_seconds": 263.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "I'll come back to the numbers."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.87,
      "end_seconds": 268.31,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Shall I start the examination?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.37,
      "end_seconds": 271.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Hold that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.67,
      "end_seconds": 286.66,
      "duration_seconds": 5.99,
      "text": "your left calf is swollen and tender, and your oxygen is lower than I'd like"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.72,
      "end_seconds": 310.97,
      "duration_seconds": 19.25,
      "text": "Alright, that's all I needed to check. Taking everything into account, this looks most like a possible blood clot in the lung. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. I'd also keep a chest infection in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 311.77,
      "end_seconds": 314.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "do you think it's something serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.43,
      "end_seconds": 330.82,
      "duration_seconds": 15.39,
      "text": "I can't promise yet but most people with a possible blood clot in the lung do well once it's treated properly let me just check I've got this right you've had sudden shortness of breath and no chest tightness"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 331.53,
      "end_seconds": 333.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "that's what happened, yes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.05,
      "end_seconds": 359.94,
      "duration_seconds": 24.89,
      "text": "We should do a CT scan of the chest for breathlessness. I'm going to order a D-dimer blood test, for possible clot. You need to go to hospital now for a scan. Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference. Let's get you seen by the medical team, I'll arrange the letter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 361.45,
      "end_seconds": 362.99,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "Alright, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.56,
      "end_seconds": 368.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "alright, I think we're done unless you have questions"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 369.78,
      "end_seconds": 374.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "good, you know, thanks, I'll see you then"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.16,
      "end_seconds": 377.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Alright, all the best."
    }
  ]
}